Atlas rescue mode

Your original disk is attached as /dev/vdb and is NOT mounted.
Inspect it first: sudo lsblk -f /dev/vdb
For a filesystem on the whole disk:
  sudo mkdir -p /mnt/original
  sudo mount /dev/vdb /mnt/original
For a partitioned disk, mount the appropriate partition instead.
Unmount a filesystem before running fsck or other offline repair tools.

Repairs written to the original disk persist after rescue ends.
Stop/Start keeps this rescue disk. Reboot or Exit Rescue discards it.
Copy any tools or notes you need before you leave rescue.
Ordinary sudo reboot reports exit to Metal and boots the original disk.
A forced reset or failed notification can leave rescue selected; use Exit Rescue.
